<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Melzi d'Eril</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1753–1816</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Melzi d'Eril was a Milanese aristocrat and statesman who served as vice-president of the Italian Republic from 1802 to 1805, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> as president. He built an effective administration, reformed finances and negotiated a concordat with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. When the republic became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1805 he became its grand chancellor, and he was later made Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-melzi-deril.jpg" alt="Francesco Melzi d'Eril" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea Appiani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melzi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
